{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116208","id":3276975687,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7DUq5H","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116208","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116208.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116208.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116208","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116208/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116208/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116208/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/65e2917ecff491b6b8ff20e084fa755126adc8e3","number":116208,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add `AnimationMixer` configuration warning on conflicting track types","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Resolves godotengine/godot-proposals#14208.\r\n\r\nThis pull request aims to improve the usability of `AnimationTree` and `AnimationPlayer`, by showing a node configuration warning if `deterministic` is enabled and there are two tracks in the `RESET` animation that both reset the same property, but using different `NodePath` specificity, e.g. `MyNode:position` and `MyNode:position:x`.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"865\" height=\"335\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/91a51f73-d263-4728-b78a-515d40a24f3f\" />\r\n\r\nThis should hopefully help catch some of the playback/blending issues that arise from mixing bezier tracks and value tracks, which is discouraged in the documentation, as seen [here](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.6/tutorials/animation/animation_track_types.html#bezier-curve-track).\r\n\r\nNote that this is a more conservative approach of a previous attempt that aimed to emit this warning for conflicts between non-`RESET` animations as well, but after seeing some questionable false positives we scaled it back to this. We'd love to hear feedback on whether there are more problematic cases we could/should include here.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":283518733,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODM1MTg3MzM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/usability","name":"usability","description":"","color":"447744","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666705648,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA1NjQ4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:animation","name":"topic:animation","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,